  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1021 PM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nBy this weekend, the high pressure shifts off to the west, and \ntemperatures will dip ever so slightly. But temperatures remaining \nin the 90s this weekend and into at least the first half of next \nweek will still be well above normal for early September. As far as \nrain goes, northwest flow will open the door for low rain chances, \nlikely diurnally-driven, to continue into this weekend and early \nnext week. Unfortunately, these hotter temperatures look to \ncontinue well into next week as ensemble guidance is favoring the \nhigh pressure to build back towards our area, keeping these above \nnormal temperatures continuing in the extended forecast.",
